---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Strider Settgast"
  description="Physics, mathematics, computation, and the ideas that connect technical fields."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>What I care about, and how I work.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        My formal training is in physics, with a minor in computational
        mathematics at Florida Institute of Technology. I'm most interested in
        problems where the important structure is not directly visible and has
        to be inferred from measurements, models, or incomplete information.
      </p>

      <p>
        What I find compelling is how often the same mathematical ideas
        reappear in different places. Inverse problems, dynamical models,
        transforms, probability, geometry, and numerical methods can show up
        in very different scientific settings while preserving much of the
        same underlying structure. I like following those connections rather
        than treating fields as isolated boxes.
      </p>

      <p>
        I tend to be drawn to open-ended technical work: learning unfamiliar
        material, building a coherent picture of a problem, and then designing
        an experiment, simulation, or system that can test that picture against
        something concrete. That has led me through scientific computing,
        machine learning, signal analysis, geometry, neuroscience, and
        quantitative modeling, with physics as the main anchor.
      </p>

      <p>
        I use computation heavily as a scientific tool, including modern
        AI-assisted development workflows. I care about using those tools to
        extend reasoning and experimentation, not to replace the need to
        understand what a model or calculation is actually saying.
      </p>

      <p>
        This site is a place for public projects and longer-form writing about
        ideas I want to work through carefully.
      </p>

      <div class="links">
        <a href={withBase('/projects')}>
          See my projects →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .container {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem;
  }

  .page-header {
    padding: 4rem 0 2.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .page-header h1 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .page-header p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  .prose {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: #333;
    max-width: 640px;
    padding: 2.5rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }

  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .links a {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
